First, make sure to install and link the `markdown-c` library in your project. You can do this by using the header headers and using the conversion function provided by the `markdown-c` library. The following is an example implementation:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <markdown-c.hpp>

std::string markdownToHtml(const std::string& markdown) {
    markdown::Markdown md;
    std::string html = md.convert(markdown);
    return html;
}

int main() {
    std::string markdown = "# Title\n\nThis is a paragraph.";
    std::string html = markdownToHtml(markdown);
    std::cout << html << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

